      "side": 1,
      "message": "The !from case is dealing with the case where the \"from\" process has died -- that\u0027s how it gets set to NULL. So you don\u0027t need to iterate -- if from\u003d\u003dNULL here then there is no one to send the extended error to. Sending it to tasks further down the stack doesn\u0027t make sense since from their PoV, it is a failure due to death of a process (which has already been processed -- hence the NULL value here).\n\nSo I think this can just be:\n```\n  static void binder_set_from_extended_error(struct binder_transaction *t,\n\t\t\t\t\t   struct binder_extended_error *ee)\n  {\n    struct binder_thread *from \u003d binder_get_txn_from_and_acq_inner(t);\n\n    if (from and from-\u003eee.command \u003d\u003d BR_OK)\n      from-\u003eee \u003d *ee;\n    binder_inner_proc_unlock(from-\u003eproc);\n    binder_thread_dec_tmpref(from);\n  }\n```",
      "revId": "470678496444690df8bd6a6cd47590f1d9cfa448",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
